# Implementation Plan - Payroll Data Extraction App

# Goal Description
Create a full-stack application (React + Python FastAPI) to upload payroll PDFs, extract data using a multi-modal LLM, and store it in a database with duplicate detection.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **LLM Provider**: The user requested a **Local LLM**. We will use **LangChain** to interface with a local provider (likely **Ollama** or similar, compatible with OpenAI API format or direct local integration). The system will be designed to easily swap models.
> **Database**: Using SQLite for simplicity.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Python/FastAPI)
#### [NEW] `backend/`
- `main.py`: Entry point.
- `models.py`: SQLAlchemy database models (PayrollEntry, UploadLog).
- `schemas.py`: Pydantic models for API request/response.
- `services/llm_service.py`: Logic to call Local LLM via LangChain.
- `services/pdf_service.py`: Logic to convert PDF to images (for vision models) or text (for text models).
- `database.py`: DB connection.

### Frontend (React/Vite)
#### [NEW] `frontend/`
- `src/App.jsx`: Main routing.
- `src/components/Dashboard.jsx`: Summary view.
- `src/components/UploadFlow.jsx`: Handle file drop, progress, and review.
- `src/api.js`: Axios setup for backend communication.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Backend unit tests for duplicate detection logic.

### Manual Verification
- Start backend server.
- Start frontend server.
- Upload the provided sample PDF `Invio Cedolino ITT ITALIA S.r.l. Ottobre 2025 (1).PDF`.
- Verify data is extracted (simulated or real).
- Confirm "Review" screen appears.
- Save data.
- Try uploading the same file again -> Expect duplicate error/warning.
